  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 0757563d82c9a675b9a99bd1508cb6227afccd0e).\n\n## What changed\n- `camcraft-cli script`, `process` and `mcp` now answer `--help` / `-h` (in any position of their arguments) with their own usage on stdout and exit 0.\n- The check runs before each lane parses its arguments, so `mcp --help` does not start the JSON-RPC server (it reads no stdin).\n- Each usage lists the arguments and flags the parser reads: script `<job.js>`; process `<job.camproj>`, `-o/--out`, `--cps`; mcp `--connect <host:port>`.\n- Top-level `help` gains a line: `camcraft-cli <command> --help`.\n- Unknown flags still exit 2. Parsing stays hand-rolled, no new dependency.\n- Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/1296-cli-subcommand-help.md`.\n\n## Tests\n- `crates/app/tests/cli.rs`:\n  - `every_subcommand_answers_help_and_names_its_flags` (each command, `--help` and `-h`: exit 0, names its flags, empty stderr)\n  - `help_flag_answers_anywhere_in_the_argv`\n  - `mcp_help_does_not_start_the_server` (a JSON-RPC initialize line gets no answer under `--help`; a plain `mcp` does answer it as a control)\n  - `unknown_flags_still_refuse_with_a_two_and_help_lists_per_command`\n- Gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on the final head (app suites cli, mcp, mcp_verify, regression_models, lib unit tests).\n- Clippy: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The CLI docs page (#1294) still says subcommands do not take `--help`; it needs a one-line update after this merges.\n- Windows/macOS builds not run here.\n\nChangelog: camcraft-cli script, process and mcp answer --help with their own usage and exit 0 (#1296)\n\nFixes #1296\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
